export anchor FocusInboxStyle:
    number: 395
    screen: EmailClient
    name: Focus inbox
    idea: The inbox leads with only the few messages that need you, set large in a quiet serif inside vast dark space, and lets everything else shrink to one soft line each.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #111214, the whole page
        well: #17181b, the two focus cards and the style sheet
        hair: #2a2b30, thin rules and card edges
        ink: #ede7dd, headings and the letter
        soft: #b3aca1, snippets, labels and folder links
        faint: #8f897f, times and small notes
        apricot: #f2b48a, the New marker, the open card edge, the Reply button and focus
        onApricot: #2a1608, text on apricot
    type:
        Two stacks. A serif, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino,
        Georgia, for the greeting at 60px, card subjects at 30px, the open
        subject at 40px and the letter at 26px with 1.55 leading. A sans,
        ui-sans-serif, Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Arial, at 16px for
        everything else, with 13px spaced capitals for small section words.
    layout:
        A single centred column about 1040px wide. A quiet top line holds
        the brand with Mail in apricot and the folders as plain text links,
        Inbox 12 underlined in apricot, then the labels each led by a hash.
        After 96px of space the greeting reads Two things need you, Mara,
        with Mara in apricot, over the line Everything else in your 12 can
        wait until after coffee. Two large rounded cards follow side by
        side for Northpass and Priya Nair, each with a hollow ring and the
        word New, the subject in serif, the quoted snippet and the sender
        and time. The Northpass card has an apricot edge and says open
        below. A section titled Can wait lists the other four messages as
        single ruled lines with sender, subject, small notes and time.
        Far below, the open message sits in two columns, a left column
        with the subject and From, To and Sent pairs, and a right column
        with the letter in large serif and round buttons for Reply,
        Reply all and Forward, then Snooze and Archive as quiet words.
        Below 900px the cards and the reader stack. On a phone everything
        is one column with the list first and the message last.
    spacing: An 8px unit used in big steps. 96px above the greeting, 72 to 120px between sections, 32px inside cards.
    density: Very sparse. Two cards, four one line rows and one letter, nothing else.
    corners: 24px focus cards, fully round buttons, square rows.
    borders: 1px #2a2b30 hairlines. The open card trades its edge for apricot.
    shadows: None at all.
    icons:
        Very few, thin 1.5 stroke at text size. New is a hollow ring plus
        the word New, starred a filled star plus Starred, labels a tag
        outline plus the name, attachments a clip plus Attachment.
    focus: A 2px apricot outline offset 4px, and fields turn their underline apricot.
    tone: One calm human sentence up top, then single words, such as Can wait, Open and New.
